      "content": "Counter the 24-month dip by emphasizing that the associated government investment in local infrastructure and R&D will drive demand for *other* related, high-value service industries in the short term. Frame the manufacturing shift not as a direct cost, but as necessary *retooling* that will make the industry more competitive globally in 3-5 years compared to current, globally reliant models. This turns the \"contraction\" into a \"strategic investment in future market advantage.\"",
